To create an interactive check-in page with popups for your church's media center, here are the steps to guide you, along with suggested corrections to your existing code:

### Code Structure
1. **HTML Structure**: Ensure that your emotion elements are structured properly. Each emotion should have its own div representing them, and ideally, popups should be separate from the clickable area.

   Example:
   ```html
   <div class="emotion" onclick="showPopup('happyPopup')">
       <p>Happy</p>
   </div>
   <div class="popup" id="happyPopup">
       <p>I praise you, for I am fearfully and wonderfully made. Wonderful are your works; my soul knows it very well. Psalm 139:14</p>
       <button onclick="hidePopup('happyPopup')">Close</button>
   </div>
   ```

2. **CSS for Popup**: Ensure that the popup is styled correctly and initially hidden. You can use CSS to control its visibility.

   Example:
   ```css
   .popup {
       display: none; /* Initially hidden */
       position: absolute;
       background-color: white;
       border: 1px solid black;
       padding: 10px;
   }

   .popup.show {
       display: block; /* Show when class is toggled */
   }
   ```

### JavaScript Functionality
3. **JavaScript for Interaction**: Modify your JavaScript function to handle showing and hiding the popups. You can use a function like `showPopup()` that adds a class to display the popup and `hidePopup()` to remove it.

   Example:
   ```javascript
   function showPopup(popupId) {
       var popup = document.getElementById(popupId);
       popup.classList.add("show");
   }

   function hidePopup(popupId) {
       var popup = document.getElementById(popupId);
       popup.classList.remove("show");
   }
   ```

### Integrating Everything
4. **Putting It All Together**: Ensure your HTML structure calls the `showPopup()` function and the buttons within the popups call `hidePopup()` to close them. 

### Final HTML Example
Here’s how all of these elements can be combined:

```html
<div class="emotion" onclick="showPopup('happyPopup')">
    <p>Happy</p>
</div>
<div class="popup" id="happyPopup">
    <p>I praise you, for I am fearfully and wonderfully made. Wonderful are your works; my soul knows it very well. Psalm 139:14</p>
    <button onclick="hidePopup('happyPopup')">Close</button>
</div>

<script>
    function showPopup(popupId) {
        var popup = document.getElementById(popupId);
        popup.classList.add("show");
    }

    function hidePopup(popupId) {
        var popup = document.getElementById(popupId);
        popup.classList.remove("show");
    }
</script>
```

